          "title": "You'll want to know: 虽然",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "虽然 — suīrán — \"although\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "虽然下雨了但是我们还是去了 suīrán xiàyǔ le dànshì wǒmen háishi qù le — Although it rained, we still went."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 虽 (suī) — nine strokes in two pieces: 口 kǒu on top, and under it an insect piece, six strokes: a small box with a vertical through it, a stroke rising along the foot, and a dot. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "虽然 (suīrán) is built from suī and 然, both inherited from Middle Chinese, swij and nyen (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first as a particle and the second as a particle and 'like this'."
            }
          ]
        },
